          { q: "Can full face Botox lift the corners of the mouth?", a: "Certain muscles affect the position of the corners of the mouth. Where the anatomy suits, treating them can be discussed. Because the mouth region is functionally complex, particularly careful dosing is required." },
          { q: "What is a lip flip?", a: "A lip flip uses a small dose of botulinum toxin in selected parts of the muscle around the upper lip. No additional volume is created, so a lip flip is not the same as a lip filler." },
          { q: "Can full face Botox be reversed?", a: "No. Botulinum toxin cannot be dissolved with hyaluronidase the way hyaluronic acid can. The effect decreases on its own over time." },
          { q: "What are the risks of full face Botox?", a: "Possible side effects include redness, bruising, headache and temporary asymmetries. Depending on the region, unwanted muscle weakness can also occur." },
          { q: "Can Botox make the eyelid drop?", a: "A temporary change in eyelid or eyebrow position is one of the possible unwanted effects of treatments in the upper face. Your individual risk is discussed before treatment." },
          { q: "What does off-label mean with full face Botox?", a: "Depending on the botulinum toxin product used, certain aesthetic facial regions can lie outside the approved indication. Such a use has to be assessed medically and explained individually." },
          { q: "How many Botox units do you need for a full face?", a: "A blanket figure would make no sense. The dose depends on the muscles treated, their strength, the medicine used and the result wanted. The unit systems of different products are also not directly transferable." },
          { q: "How often should full face Botox be repeated?", a: "A repeat should follow the return of relevant muscle activity and a fresh analysis. Not every region has to be re-treated at the same interval automatically." },
          { q: "Is full face Botox suitable for men?", a: "Suitability does not depend on gender alone. Muscle strength, anatomy and the treatment goal are decisive. With stronger musculature, a different dosing concept can be necessary." },
          { q: "From what age does full face Botox make sense?", a: "There is no general ideal starting age. What matters is the muscle activity present, your specific treatment goals and your suitability – not a particular age." },
          { q: "Can full face Botox be done during pregnancy or breastfeeding?", a: "Aesthetic botulinum toxin treatments are not routinely carried out during pregnancy or breastfeeding. Pregnancy or breastfeeding should be mentioned before planning begins." },
          { q: "What does full face Botox cost at AS Clinic Berlin?", a: "The cost depends on which regions are actually treated, which product is used and what individual dose is required. The specific treatment plan and price are discussed before treatment." },
          { q: "Where can I have full face Botox in Berlin?", a: "AS Clinic offers consultations on full face Botox at Kurfürstendamm 102 in Berlin-Charlottenburg. Before treatment, the muscle activity of the whole face is analysed and a treatment plan is drawn up on that basis." }
